ll production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. (v2.3.1-rc was only healthy in staging, so it was not used.) After the rollback, the service reports healthy and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying it.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 15009, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_013LmzDuBvv6JdYXV8RpcBku", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 15009, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_013LmzDuBvv6JdYXV8RpcBku", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18492, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in every region, and it's healthy again. I also opened incident INC-0001 as a SEV2, which paged on-call.\n\n- **What was wrong:** The latest release, v2.3.1, was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with about 18% of requests erroring.\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1-rc is newer, but it was only ever healthy in staging, so I didn't use it.\n- **After the rollback:** All three regions are now on v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback and the result. As a follow-up, it says the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure should be found before v2.3.1 is deployed again.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01GsRc5CMmGxVJZUL1zdcrf1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_016BPkeiAM3pNJ1CmMmrU6K7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1-rc was only healthy in staging, so it doesn't count.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01YXYgaWmn2eSFVnS4y3C9qm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01V9y2BVwQnhk8NxVJ9Rg4dC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01HGE24ubuMaa93ob6434EZJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_013LmzDuBvv6JdYXV8RpcBku", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the deploy of checkout-api v2.3.1 to production, health checks failed in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) and the error rate was about 18%. checkout-api was rolled back in all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. (v2.3.1-rc was only healthy in staging, so it was not used.) After the rollback, the service reports healthy and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before redeploying it.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in every region, and it's healthy again. I also opened incident INC-0001 as a SEV2, which paged on-call.\n\n- **What was wrong:** The latest release, v2.3.1, was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with about 18% of requests erroring.\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1-rc is newer, but it was only ever healthy in staging, so I didn't use it.\n- **After the rollback:** All three regions are now on v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback and the result. As a follow-up, it says the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure should be found before v2.3.1 is deployed again.", "type": "text"}]}]}